hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17656","Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah, who said: al-'Abbas entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we go out and see Quraysh talking, and when they see us they fall silent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry, and a vein between his eyes swelled. Then he said: By Allah, faith will not enter the heart of a person until they love you for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and for my kinship."
"17657","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Yazid, meaning Ibn 'Ata', narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal: 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib narrated to me, who said: al-'Abbas entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angry, and he said to him: What angers you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is it with us and Quraysh? When they meet among themselves they meet with cheerful faces, and when they meet us they meet us with other than that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until his face reddened and a vein between his eyes swelled, and when he became angry it swelled. When it passed from him, he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, or he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, faith will not enter the heart of a man until they love you for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and for His Messenger. Then he said: O people, whoever harms al-'Abbas has harmed me; the uncle of a man is like his father."
"17658","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Yazid ibn 'Ata' narrated to us, from Yazid, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, who said: Some people from the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We hear from your people such that one of them says: The likeness of Muhammad is but like a palm tree grown in a dungheap. Husayn said: al-Kiba' is refuse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, who am I? They said: You are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I am Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib. He said: We never heard him trace his lineage before it. Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created His creation and made me from the best of His creation. Then He divided them into two divisions and made me from the better of the two divisions. Then He made them tribes and made me from the best tribe among them. Then He made them houses and made me from the best house among them. And I am the best of you in house and the best of you in self, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17659","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith, that he and al-Fadl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to have him marry them and employ them over charity so they would gain from that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This charity is but the filth of people, and it is not lawful for Muhammad nor for the family of Muhammad. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Mahmiyah al-Zubaydi: Marry al-Fadl, and said to Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib: Marry 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah. And he said to Mahmiyah ibn Juz' al-Zubaydi, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to employ him over the fifths, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to give dowry on their behalf from the fifth, something which 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith did not name. And at the beginning of this hadith, 'Ali met them and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will not employ you. They said: This is your envy. He said: I am Abu Hasan of the people; I will not move until I see what he replies to you. When they spoke to him, he was silent, and Zaynab kept waving her garment that it concerned your need."
"17660","Ya'qub and Sa'd said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from al-Zuhri, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, who informed him that 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib informed him that Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith and 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib gathered and said: By Allah, if only we sent these two boys, and he said to me and to al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he put them in charge of these charities, so they would render what people render and gain the benefit people gain. While they were concerning that, 'Ali ibn Abi Talib came and said: What do you intend? They told him what they intended. He said: Do not do it, for by Allah he will not do it. They said: Why do you do this? This from you is but jealousy toward us; you accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and attained his kinship by marriage, and we did not envy you for that. He said: I am Abu Hasan; send them. Then he lay down. He said: When he prayed Zuhr, we preceded him to the chamber and stood at it until he passed by us. He took our hands, then said: Bring out what you are concealing. He entered, and we entered with him, and he was then in the house of Zaynab bint Jahsh. He said: We spoke to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we came to you to put us in charge of these charities, so we gain the benefit people gain and render to you what people render. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent and raised his head toward the ceiling of the house until we wanted to speak to him. He said: Zaynab gestured to us from behind her veil as though forbidding us from speaking to him. He turned and said: Indeed charity is not befitting for Muhammad nor for the family of Muhammad; it is but the filth of people. Call Mahmiyah ibn Juz' for me, and he was in charge of the tenths, and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith. They came, and he said to Mahmiyah: Give dowry on their behalf from the fifth."
"17661","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith, who said: al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib and Ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith gathered in the mosque, and he mentioned the hadith."
